Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Refractors Gouge the Low Cloud
- Story & Context: When the wedding brawl broke out in the sawdust, Jack and Clara hauled two sodden Fender Jaguars up the fire escape to the roof above Blackpool's promenade to settle their family feud in decibels. Smelling of spilt stout, cheap carnations, and damp canvas, Jack kicked his spring-reverb tank across the lead guttering until it rattled like collapsing bleachers, bellowing into the freezing drizzle while Clara tore through a frantic, minor-key surf vamp that out-screamed the police sirens below. "Look up, you dogs, the stars don't want your ring," sneered Jack into an open telescope tube turned makeshift microphone, igniting a sound built on runaway bridal fury.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: High-contrast film still looking upward through a fractured brass telescope lens toward a bruised plum-colored night sky, raindrops streaking across the glass, framed by the silhouette of a jagged slate rooftop and an electric guitar neck pointed at the clouds.

Track 2: Madeline Vane Behind the Water Tower
- Story & Context: Huddled behind a rusted zinc cistern four stories above the pier, the groom’s estranged aunt Madeline tuned her hollow-body guitar with rusty pliers while nursing a cracked collarbone sustained during the cake-cutting melee. With coastal sleet dissolving the theatrical clown grease on her cheeks, she picked a bitter, chiming Britpop progression against the distant thud of North Sea waves, confessing to the circling seagulls that she had poured battery acid into the menagerie generator before the ceremony even started. "I kept the ledger and I buried the dress," she drawled into her scratchplate, her wet twang dissolving into the metallic rattle of rooftop exhaust flues.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Atmospheric cinematic shot of a gaunt woman in running clown makeup and a soaked tailored mod parka sitting against a corrugated iron water tank, holding a cherry-red hollow-body guitar, looking through an antique amateur brass star-finder at a roof-top view of stormy ocean surf.

Track 3: Charivaria Under Cassiopeia
- Story & Context: By daybreak, both circus clans abandoned their weapons and climbed up the gables to perform the traditional shivaree ritual for the ruined marriage, pressing unamplified guitar pickups against the rooftop iron railings to harvest the building's electrical hum. Amidst the sickening smell of wet lion blankets and boiling seaside tea, the rival players locked into a monolithic, unhinged surf-tremolo drone directed straight at the circumpolar constellations, daring the sky to collapse on their feuding heads. "Ring down the curtain, the bridegroom is ghost-bound," yelled the chorus of shivering acrobats, cementing the rooftop vigil as a mythic rite for doomed lovers across the British coast.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Eerie, melancholic album art showing an entire circus troupe huddled atop chimney pots at dawn beneath a pale, star-flecked sky, vintage electric guitars raised skyward like lightning rods, with fog rising from the cold ocean below.

